# Production secrets — NEVER track (Sec audit H15). Real values live only on the
# server in /opt/doergo/infra/docker/.env.production (untracked).
.env.production
infra/docker/.env.production

# Working scratch at repo root — screenshots, exported PDFs, and audit/planning
# notes that don't belong in the repo. Globs are root-anchored so nested assets
# aren't affected; tracked root files are re-included below.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.pdf
!/Doergo.pdf
/docs/archive/root-plans/local-only/

# Local backup / scratch directories
docs/dashboard-spaces-backup/
emails/
apps/api/gateway/uploads/

# Build output of tools/blog-mcp — 6 MB, rebuildable from the source beside it.
tools/blog-mcp.zip

# Source design exports — the Figma/Illustrator output the UI was drawn from,
# plus a zip of each folder sitting next to the folder itself. 63MB, 54 files,
# referenced by nothing in apps/, infra/, packages/, tools/ or docs/: git was
# being used as a file share for binaries that never diff. Kept on disk, and
# belong wherever design source belongs.
doergo design/

# The sales brochures — four hand-made PDF exports, ~10.7MB, built by no
# script and read by no code. A brochure is a deliverable, but a re-export is
# a whole new 2.7MB blob git keeps forever, and the current one is only ever
# wanted wherever it is actually sent from.
docs/archive/marketing/sales-brochure*.pdf

# App screenshots — 8.8MB of PNGs regenerated by the capture sweep, and the
# kind of binary that just cost this repo 719MB of history. Keep them on disk.
store-listing/screenshots/app-sweep/

# Time explainer captures (heavy, regenerated by time-explainer/stills.ts)
tools/video/time-explainer/stills/

# Video voice-overs and music: large binaries, kept out of git like the finished mp4s.
tools/video/**/*.wav
tools/video/**/*.mp3
tools/video/**/*.m4a

# Never committed (owner's rule): design mockups and reports with their voice-overs, the confidential Fletzberger
# CRM handover, the partner pitch video, and session notes. Files under docs/design already in git stay tracked.
docs/design/
HBC_FIELD_QUELLCODE_FLETZBERGER/
HBC_FIELD_WEB_APPLICATION/
tools/video/partner-pitch/
SESSION_*.md
